s denoted by:","options":["x̄","σ","N or Σf","μ"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Advanced Interpretation"}},{"itemId":"641d7c71-a246-5aa3-a725-494ba7b12bb5","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"67ce26b3-052e-413c-a05d-8e7d28e5017f","sourceKey":"quiz:9","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"A descriptive measure calculated from a population is called a:","options":["Statistic","Parameter","Variable","Sample mean"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Basic Concepts & Data Collection"}},{"itemId":"33c058a7-b947-58de-84da-abe28395024f","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"ae65e662-546a-417b-a7dd-93b252301fa4","sourceKey":"quiz:90","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"A distribution with two modes is called:","options":["Unimodal","Bimodal","Multimodal","Normal"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Advanced Interpretation"}},{"itemId":"f6b5bb1e-091b-5461-bac9-000292e00680","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"27847c6a-ec27-4baa-8d2f-12c7d3088147","sourceKey":"quiz:91","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"What is the class mark for the interval 10-20?","options":["10","15","20","30"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Advanced Interpretation"}},{"itemId":"5772f224-a902-5166-8e2d-d45640fcf9ea","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"48f70939-86b8-4b78-8c79-c0afd3b561aa","sourceKey":"quiz:92","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"If N=100, the position of the median is:","options":["50th","25th","100th","1st"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Advanced Interpretation"}},{"itemId":"1bc12fe9-8395-57ff-8c0c-00db92d45f46","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"a52f8caa-0e03-4c9d-a699-b127e9aa4677","sourceKey":"quiz:93","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following cannot be negative?","options":["Mean","Median","Standard Deviation","Skewness"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Advanced Interpretation"}},{"itemId":"0ee54516-f9fa-5c66-9a94-e27ead92a840","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"fb46977f-e491-4944-9072-b4be5780e286","sourceKey":"quiz:94","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"The \"empirical rule\" applies to which distribution?","options":["Binomial","Normal","Poisson","Uniform"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Advanced Interpretation"}},{"itemId":"38566817-33e7-5ba7-b4c9-4da6ace1dd55","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"5477cf13-d0f2-4363-a748-0f6b9627e1bf","sourceKey":"quiz:95","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"The range of the set {7, 7, 7, 7} is:","options":["7","0","1","4"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Advanced Interpretation"}},{"itemId":"1bc8e79d-b468-5ced-9cc3-50194543a41c","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"1e266ada-6bce-445d-af4d-13b98fec051d","sourceKey":"quiz:96","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"In the formula for the Mean, Σ stands for:","options":["Sample","Summation (add all)","Standard","Square"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Advanced Interpretation"}},{"itemId":"10b56f53-d7cd-58a4-86f0-9f22e91d240b","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"4913096c-d5b4-4790-93db-24ac86633e37","sourceKey":"quiz:97","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Deciles divide data into how many parts?","options":["4","10","100","2"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Advanced Interpretation"}},{"itemId":"a3d99069-143c-5595-a439-eef5cb4ae96c","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"3e37e641-28cc-46a3-b070-5af6a092ebbc","sourceKey":"quiz:98","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Primary data is generally more ________ than secondary data.","options":["Expensive","Reliable (for specific use)","Time-consuming","All of the above"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Advanced Interpretation"}},{"itemId":"2f7eba3b-dc23-582d-af25-4ff118d14103","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"85af4b6f-c531-45de-bcc8-a0242322d2d8","sourceKey":"quiz:99","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"The probability of picking a Red card from a standard deck is:","options":["1/4","1/2","1/13","1/52"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Advanced Interpretation"}}]$expected_content$::jsonb,
