ion","questionId":"c4796d92-a00b-4b01-b809-bc5540a40d27","sourceKey":"quiz:455","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following philosophers defined humans as political animals?","options":["Aristotle","Socrates","Plato","Epicurus"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Master Question Bank","explanation":"Aristotle's Politics famously describes man as a political animal."}},{"itemId":"5323c376-de51-5021-92fb-4ee9c334b88e","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000013","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"83f9bdd8-30e2-43ba-adf0-a5fabc4ae4c1","sourceKey":"quiz:456","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"The definition of Philosophy suggests:","options":["An attempt to acquire knowledge","Merely learning history","A set of rigid religious doctrines","Uncritical belief systems"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Master Question Bank","explanation":"Philosophy is broadly framed as humanity's attempt to acquire organized knowledge and understanding."}},{"itemId":"991e35a9-e18c-5a27-b9a1-db27ae62f131","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000013","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"47d9eaea-7e25-4bc4-9620-0cedc497b6d6","sourceKey":"quiz:457","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"The questions “What is mind?” and “Does God exist?” can be linked to the branch of philosophy called:","options":["Epistemology","Ethics","Logic","Metaphysics"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Master Question Bank","explanation":"Questions about mind and God's existence fall under Metaphysics."}},{"itemId":"6180e1ee-db04-5075-b0de-6cf307ee10f2","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000013","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"9fd04ea1-febe-4502-b352-dc1d66965f67","sourceKey":"quiz:458","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"prompt":"The Greek term “episteme” is associated with:","options":["Opinion","Beauty","Craft","Knowledge"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Master Question Bank","explanation":"Episteme is the Greek root for knowledge, givi