  where kind = 'course_overview') = $expected_content$[{"itemId":"aacda638-71d7-590e-9728-205fc7214117","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014","kind":"course_overview","questionId":null,"sourceKey":"course-overview","parentItemId":null,"revision":1,"payload":{"title":"Introduction to Financial Management","body":"A quantitative course in financial decision-making built around a single problems-and-solutions workbook (Abass A. Shiro). The course progresses from the time value of money through investment appraisal (with certainty, risk, rationing, inflation, and tax), the cost of capital and leverage, working capital management, portfolio theory, dividend policy, and financial statement analysis, before moving into capital market instruments — bond valuation and the Capital Asset Pricing Model. Two topics on the official course outline (market efficiency; pension funds, mutual funds, and the structure of the money management industry) are not covered in the prescribed workbook and appear to require separate lecture material. Fin 101 introduction to finance.","topics":[{"chapter":"1","description":"Financial Ratio Analysis"},{"chapter":"2","description":"Mathematics of Finance"},{"chapter":"3","description":"Analysis of Risk and Return"},{"chapter":"4","description":"Working Capital Management"},{"chapter":"5","description":"Capital Asset Pricing Model"},{"chapter":"6","description":"Net Present Value"},{"chapter":"7","description":"Market Efficiency"},{"chapter":"8","description":"Pension Funds, Mutual Funds, Structure of Money Management Industry"},{"chapter":"9","description":"Bonds and Interest Rate Forwards, Futures and Options"}],"examFocus":["The difference between ordinary annuity and annuity due, and correctly identifying which applies to a given cash flow pattern","Continuous compounding versus discrete compounding, and computing the effective annual rate from a nominal rate","Resolving NPV/IRR conflicts for mutually exclusive projects with differing cash flow timing — and why NPV is the theoretically preferred criterion","Sensitivity margin calculations for sales, cost, and asset price in a capital budgeting decision, and the method's key limitation","Using the risk-free (treasury bill) rate, not the risk-adjusted cost of capital, to discount expected cash flows when computing Expected NPV","Coefficient of variation versus standard deviation as the correct basis for choosing between investments of different scale for a risk-averse investor","The Economic Order Quantity (EOQ) formula, and correctly separating ordering/carrying cost (controllable) from purchase cost (largely fixed)","The cash discount cost formula — [%disc ÷ (100 − %disc)] × [365 ÷ (max payment period − discount period)] — and its sensitivity to the assumed days-in-year convention (360 vs 365)","Computing a firm's working capital cycle in days from stock, debtor, WIP, and creditor turnover periods","Portfolio return as a weighted average of individual security returns, versus portfolio risk, which is NOT a simple weighted average once correlation is introduced","Identifying the minimum-risk portfolio weighting, which is rarely a 100% holding in either security","How positive correlation between two securities reduces the diversification benefit of combining them","The four major categories of financial ratio (liquidity, profitability/efficiency, long-term solvency and stability, stock market/investor) and which ratios belong to each","Correctly identifying all components of current liabilities in a ratio question — tax payable is often a hidden addition to trade creditors, not stated as a separate line","Bond valuation with semi-annual coupons — the periodic discount rate must be halved (Kd ÷ 2) and the number of periods doubled (2n); watch for workbook solutions that inconsistently apply this","The CAPM formula E(Ri) = Rf + [E(Rm) − Rf]×Bi, and the decision rule for over-priced versus under-priced securities based on comparing given return to CAPM-required return","Systematic (unavoidable, market-wide) versus unsystematic (avoidable, firm-specific) risk, and Beta as the proxy for systematic risk in CAPM"]}}]$expected_content$::jsonb,
